  "limitations": [
    "Small 60-event sample, only one target day per event; not nationwide validation.",
    "Only 5 positive cells across 5 validation fires supported both model selection and calibration/threshold fitting. Those choices are especially unstable; independent-test Brier error is worse than smoothed persistence.",
    "Label absence means no retained satellite detection, not known absence of burning; cloud validity is unavailable.",
    "Historical finalized gridMET and retrospectively compiled fire masks do not prove operational data availability or calibration.",
    "Live terrain product, GFS provider/lead aggregation, publication latency and changing satellite operations introduce transfer error.",
    "Fuel structure, live/dead fuel moisture, suppression, spotting, human and lightning ignition processes are not modeled completely.",
    "Not an official warning, perimeter, flame arrival time, crew allocation, or evacuation product."
  ],
